@startuml
title ProofSieve | Deliver an approved operation
hide footbox

actor "Authorized caller" as Caller
participant "ProofSieve Guard" as Guard
database "Decision and\ndelivery journal" as Journal
participant "Fixed HTTPS\nreceiver" as Receiver

Caller -> Guard: POST to a configured decision endpoint\nwith data and operationId
Guard -> Guard: Match original request bytes to the parsed input\nand evaluate the saved rule
alt Denied or indeterminate
    Guard -> Journal: Record the decision
    alt Decision recorded
        Journal --> Guard: Decision ID
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 403 or 503 · not_forwarded
    else Journal unavailable
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · evidence_unavailable
    end
else Approved
    Guard -> Journal: Match the existing operation or atomically\nrecord approval and reserve delivery
    alt Same key with different approved input
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 409 · operation_conflict
    else Matching reservation and retained decision
        Guard --> Caller: Original decision ID and rule version\nwith current delivery state
    else Matching reservation and expired decision
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 409 · operation_evidence_expired
    else Journal unavailable
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · evidence_unavailable
    else New reservation
        Journal --> Guard: New decision and pending delivery IDs
        Guard -> Receiver: One POST with the original JSON bytes\nService bearer and Idempotency-Key
        alt Receiver acknowledges with 2xx
            Receiver --> Guard: HTTP 2xx
            Guard -> Journal: Record delivered and receiver status
            Guard --> Caller: HTTP 200 · delivered
        else Receiver returns 3xx through 5xx
            Receiver --> Guard: HTTP 3xx–5xx
            Guard -> Journal: Record rejected and receiver status
            Guard --> Caller: HTTP 502 · rejected
        else No confirmed response
            Guard -> Journal: Record unknown
            Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · unknown
        end
    end
end

note over Guard, Journal
  If the final journal write fails, the caller receives
  HTTP 503 / unknown. The prior reservation blocks
  automatic retransmission.
end note
@enduml
